# The reference corpus: ~8.8 MB of third-party documentation (Zama, OpenZeppelin,
# PoolTogether) fetched verbatim as a local reading corpus. Not committed, because
# publishing verbatim copies of someone else's docs to a public repository is a
# different act from keeping them on disk to read, and it is not this repo's call
# to make. `git add -A` swept them in once; this stops that recurring. Remove this
# line if the decision is to publish them.
bundle/

# --- out/ : evidence yes, keys never -------------------------------------
#
# out/ is ignored because it holds LIVE PRIVATE KEYS: demo-participants.json is
# a bare array of them, and arms-c.json carries them under arms[].pk controlling
# funded Sepolia accounts. Neither has ever been committed and neither ever
# should be.
#
# But the docs cite this directory 100+ times — out/deployment.json alone is
# referenced 53 times — and a citation pointing at a file nobody can open is
# exactly the failure the September audit found elsewhere. So the evidence is
# committed and the keys are not.
#
# This is an ALLOWLIST. Adding a file here means screening it first:
#   node scripts/check-out-artifacts.mjs
# which refuses anything with a 64-hex value in a bare array or under a
# key/pk/secret field.
!out/abi-deposit.json
!out/abi-redeem.json
!out/accrue-cost.json
!out/batcher-src.txt
!out/cd-exercise.json
